  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dufatanye Kubaka Ubutabera (DKU)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  ..Rwandans seeking access to justice face two main problems: a lack of legal aid providers for poor and marginalized groups and a lack of sufficient courtrooms to hear cases. Combined with actions to contain the Covid pandemic, the case backlog and time to adjudicate cases in Rwanda increased dramatically, effectively reducing access to justice. .. ..With FY 2022 resources, Dufatanye Kubaka Ubutabera (DKU), or the &quot;Rule of Law&quot; activity, will train justice system actors to use the electronic case management system, support legal aid provision (especially for marginalized groups), and strengthen alternative dispute resolution mechanisms, including the Abunzi Mediation Committees. (Note: Abunzi are a hybrid form of justice combining traditional with modern methods of conflict resolution.) Funds will also provide training and materials to increase citizens&apos; awareness of their rights and methods of legal recourse. The activity will also support victims of gender-based violence by providing them with legal aid services and representation. DKU will not provide direct training to Government of Rwanda actors... ..By increasing the efficiency of the Rwandan justice system and access to justice, DKU directly supports USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy Development Objective 4, &quot;Increased Government Responsiveness to Citizen Priorities.&quot;.......</narrative>
  </description>
